# One contributor's harness configuration: the subagent profiles that work
# this project's own board, the permission rules that guard the operator's
# live data, and the always-on rule file that points at both. They are
# untracked because they configure a machine rather than the project. Every
# one of them names absolute paths under one home directory, so a second
# contributor cloning this repository would get twelve agents addressing
# directories that do not exist, and this repository is public. Tracking them
# also put files no compiler reads under the prose and vocabulary guards,
# which failed a continuous integration run on pull request 273 over the word
# benchmarks. Untracked on the operator's ruling of 2026-09-17.
/.devin/
/AGENTS.md

# The workbench this project's own development runs on. Its files are data
# rather than source: every claim, move and comment rewrites them, so tracking
# them turned ordinary board traffic into repository history and made the board
# unusable from the checkout, because the trunk refuses a direct push and a
# card cannot wait for a pull request to move. Untracked on the operator's
# ruling of 2026-09-14, to be revisited if the board ever needs to be shared.
/.dinah/

# The VS Code extension. The /bin/ entry above is root-anchored and does not
# reach editors/vscode/bin/, which is the staging directory one platform
# binary is copied into just before vsce packages that platform's vsix.
editors/vscode/node_modules/
editors/vscode/dist/
editors/vscode/out/
editors/vscode/bin/
editors/vscode/*.vsix
editors/vscode/vsix/
editors/vscode/.binaries/
editors/vscode/.release-binaries/
editors/vscode/src/generated/
editors/vscode/.vscode-test/
.codex/config.toml
.codex/hooks.json
